sdks/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdks/typescript#installation","content":"The SDK compiles to `dist/` before it can be referenced, run its `build` script once in the SDK folder, then add it to your project by path:"},"12":{"id":"/sdks/typescript-8","page_id":"/sdks/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdks/typescript#quick-start","content":"Create one client and reuse it. Configure its behaviour through `ClientOptions`."},"13":{"id":"/sdks/typescript-9","page_id":"/sdks/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdks/typescript#quick-start","content":"Nothing in `ClientOptions` is required, `new RecallReachPublicApiClient()` compiles, and each option left out falls back to its default. This API declares one environment, so there is no environment to select and no host to state at the construction site."},"14":{"id":"/sdks/typescript-10","page_id":"/sdks/typescript","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/sdks/typescript#from-commonjs","content":"The package ships both dialects from a single entry, so `require` works with full types. In a TypeScript CommonJS file use the `import ... = require(...)` form, a plain destructuring `require` runs fine but gives you `any`."},"15":{"id":"/api/openapi/check/checkRecall","page_id":"/api/openapi/check/checkRecall","type":"page","content":"Check a product title or model against CPSC recalls","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Home","API Reference","Check"],"tags":[],"url":"/api/openapi/check/checkRecall"},"16":{"id":"/api/openapi/check/checkRecall-0","page_id":"/api/openapi/check/checkRecall","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/api/openapi/check/checkRecall","content":"Runs the rules a shop's sales get on the text you send. Our code doesn't store or log it. It travels in the page address, so the web host's request logs may include it. At least one of title and model is needed. Limited to 60 checks an hour per visitor."},"17":{"id":"/api/openapi/check/mcpNoStream","page_id":"/api/openapi/check/mcpNoStream","type":"page","content"